## 2. Formal Propositional Calculus and Inference Derivations

Logical systems govern hardware circuit switching, assertion proofs, and deterministic control flow:

* **Inference by Modus Tollens:**
  $$\frac{P \implies Q, \quad \neg Q}{\therefore \neg P}$$
  Denying the consequent guarantees that the antecedent cannot hold, protecting software architectures from unreachable edge conditions.
* **The Law of Detachment (Modus Ponens):**
  $$((P \implies Q) \wedge P) \implies Q$$
* **De Morgan’s Dualities:**
  $$\neg(P \wedge Q) \equiv \neg P \vee \neg Q, \qquad \neg(P \vee Q) \equiv \neg P \wedge \neg Q$$

